          <h3 class="module-title">0. Bootcamp Overview &amp; Lecture Slide Decks</h3>
          <p>
            Developed and taught for the <strong>2021 Sogang University SW Summer Camp (funded by Hyundai Mobis)</strong>, this 8-module bootcamp walks you from bare-metal microSD bring-up to real-time TensorRT object detection and custom SSD transfer learning on the <strong>NVIDIA Jetson Nano</strong> (4 GB) with a Raspberry Pi CSI Camera Module V2. Download the four lecture slide decks below before starting Module 1.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Upstream Reference Repository:</strong> <a href="https://github.com/dusty-nv/jetson-inference" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color:var(--accent); font-weight:600;"><code>dusty-nv/jetson-inference</code> (Two Days to a Demo / Hello AI World)</a></li>
            <li><strong>Prerequisites:</strong> Working familiarity with Python 3, Linux command-line navigation, and SSH.</li>
          </ul>
          <div class="resource-row">
            <a class="res-pill" href="https://drive.google.com/file/d/1hRKIFkosVdGZIryZrfJZmboZXb2pbvWW/view?usp=sharing" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Lecture Deck 1 (Intro &amp; Setup PDF) ↗</a>
            <a class="res-pill" href="https://drive.google.com/file/d/1YgQVt8epuJTxlLZAzZZvvwaDla-v3qE-/view?usp=sharing" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Lecture Deck 2 (Linux &amp; Docker PDF) ↗</a>
            <a class="res-pill" href="https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Z_7mnC-ubYUkrJxy84TmE4-XdPY9YAaL/view?usp=sharing" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Lecture Deck 3 (Object Detection PDF) ↗</a>
            <a class="res-pill" href="https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ukS_5bt4VkaJ0Dd5XPxXV3uAqbNckNHZ/view?usp=sharing" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Lecture Deck 4 (Transfer Learning PDF) ↗</a>
            <a class="res-pill" href="https://github.com/dusty-nv/jetson-inference" target="_blank" rel="noopener">dusty-nv/jetson-inference Repo ↗</a>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article id="jetson-1-prep" class="module-card">
          <div class="module-header">
            <span class="module-badge">Module 1 • Hardware, JetPack 4.5, Headless VNC &amp; CSI Camera</span>
            <span style="font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:11.5px; color:var(--text-muted);">Etcher • PuTTY • vino-server • GStreamer</span>
          </div>
          <h3 class="module-title">1. Flash JetPack 4.5, Enable Headless VNC &amp; Test the CSI Camera (1. Jetson Nano 준비)</h3>
          <p>
            <strong>Step 1 · Flash the JetPack 4.5 microSD image:</strong> Download the official NVIDIA JetPack 4.5 image and write it onto a 32 GB or 64 GB microSD card with <strong>Balena Etcher</strong>. Dismiss any Windows "Format Disk" prompts after verification completes.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Step 2 · Boot headless over USB Serial and enable VNC:</strong> If you do not attach an HDMI monitor, connect the Jetson Nano Micro-USB port to your Windows PC, locate the USB Serial COM port under <strong>Device Manager → Ports (COM &amp; LPT)</strong>, and open a <code>115200</code>-baud serial session in <strong>PuTTY</strong> to finish first-boot Ubuntu setup. Next, SSH into <code>192.168.55.1</code> (port 22) over USB Ethernet and enable the <code>vino-server</code> desktop service:
          </p>

          <div class="cmd-block">
            <div class="cmd-top">
              <span>Enable VNC Server (vino) &amp; Virtual Framebuffer Resolution on Jetson Nano</span>
              <button class="copy-btn" onclick="copyCmd(this)">Copy</button>
            </div>
            <pre>cd /usr/lib/systemd/user/graphical-session.target.wants
sudo ln -s ../vino-server.service ./.
gsettings set org.gnome.Vino prompt-enabled false
gsettings set org.gnome.Vino require-encryption false
gsettings set org.gnome.Vino authentication-methods "['vnc']"
gsettings set org.gnome.Vino vnc-password $(echo -n 'thepassword'|base64)
sudo reboot

# After reboot, set virtual desktop resolution via SSH before opening VNC Viewer:
export DISPLAY=:0
xrandr --fb 1000x400</pre>
          </div>

          <p>
            <strong>Step 3 · Connect Wi-Fi and test the CSI camera:</strong> Join a Wi-Fi network from the terminal with <code>nmcli</code>, verify that <code>/dev/video0</code> is present, and stream live video from the Raspberry Pi CSI Camera V2 using <code>nvarguscamerasrc</code> GStreamer pipelines:
          </p>

          <div class="cmd-block">
            <div class="cmd-top">
              <span>Wi-Fi Connection (nmcli) &amp; CSI Camera GStreamer Test</span>
              <button class="copy-btn" onclick="copyCmd(this)">Copy</button>
            </div>
            <pre># Connect to Wi-Fi from terminal
nmcli dev wifi list
sudo nmcli --ask dev wifi connect &lt;SSID&gt;
sudo apt-get update &amp;&amp; sudo apt-get install nano

# Check CSI Camera device node (/dev/video0)
ls -l /dev/video0

# Test live CSI camera feed on desktop (Mode 0: 3280x2464, Mode 1: resized 60fps)
gst-launch-1.0 nvarguscamerasrc sensor_mode=0 ! nvoverlaysink
gst-launch-1.0 nvarguscamerasrc sensor_mode=1 ! 'video/x-raw(memory:NVMM),width=1280, height=720, framerate=60/1, format=NV12' ! nvvidconv flip-method=0 ! 'video/x-raw,width=400, height=300' ! nvvidconv ! nvegltransform ! nveglglessink -e</pre>
          </div>

          <div class="video-grid">
            <div class="video-box">
              <div class="v-label"><span>Reference: Installing VNC on Jetson Nano</span><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ch1NKfER0oM" target="_blank" rel="noopener">YouTube ↗</a></div>
              <div class="video-aspect"><iframe src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/Ch1NKfER0oM?rel=0" title="Jetson Nano VNC Setup" loading="lazy" allowfullscreen></iframe></div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article id="jetson-2-docker" class="module-card">
          <div class="module-header">
            <span class="module-badge">Module 2 • Linux CLI &amp; jetson-inference Docker Container</span>
            <span style="font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:11.5px; color:var(--text-muted);">docker/run.sh • video-viewer csi://0</span>
          </div>
          <h3 class="module-title">2. Clone jetson-inference &amp; Launch the Docker Runtime (2. Linux 및 Docker Container)</h3>
          <p>
            Avoid compiling CUDA, TensorRT, and PyTorch from source on the microSD card by running the prebuilt <code>jetson-inference</code> Docker image. Clone the repository with submodules, run <code>docker/run.sh</code> to mount the CSI camera socket and host directories automatically, and verify live camera rendering inside the container:
          </p>

          <div class="cmd-block">
            <div class="cmd-top">
              <span>Clone jetson-inference &amp; Verify Real-Time CSI Stream Inside Docker</span>
              <button class="copy-btn" onclick="copyCmd(this)">Copy</button>
            </div>
            <pre>git clone --recursive https://github.com/dusty-nv/jetson-inference
cd jetson-inference
docker/run.sh

# Inside the Docker container (# prompt), test live CSI camera display:
