        <article id="jetson-3-detectnet" class="module-card">
          <div class="module-header">
            <span class="module-badge">Module 3 • Real-Time Object Detection (SSD-MobileNet-v2)</span>
            <span style="font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:11.5px; color:var(--text-muted);">91-Class MS COCO • TensorRT FP16</span>
          </div>
          <h3 class="module-title">3. Run SSD-MobileNet-v2 Object Detection with TensorRT (3. Object Detection)</h3>
          <p>
            Run 91-class MS COCO object detection on static images and the live CSI camera feed using <code>ssd-mobilenet-v2</code>. On first launch, TensorRT compiles an FP16 engine optimized for the Jetson Nano Maxwell GPU and caches the serialized engine file on disk so subsequent runs start within seconds:
          </p>

          <div class="cmd-block">
            <div class="cmd-top">
              <span>Static Image &amp; Real-Time CSI Camera Object Detection (Inside Docker)</span>
              <button class="copy-btn" onclick="copyCmd(this)">Copy</button>
            </div>
            <pre>cd /jetson-inference/build/aarch64/bin

# 1. Detect objects on static image and save annotated output
./detectnet.py --network=ssd-mobilenet-v2 images/peds_0.jpg images/test/output.jpg

# 2. Real-time object detection on live CSI camera stream
./detectnet.py --network=ssd-mobilenet-v2 --input-width=400 --input-height=300 csi://0</pre>
          </div>

          <p>
            Implement the same detection loop in a standalone 15-line Python script with <code>jetson.inference</code> and <code>jetson.utils</code>:
          </p>

          <div class="cmd-block">
            <div class="cmd-top">
              <span>Minimal 15-Line Python Object Detection Loop (detectnet.py Core Pattern)</span>
              <button class="copy-btn" onclick="copyCmd(this)">Copy</button>
            </div>
            <pre>import jetson.inference
import jetson.utils

net = jetson.inference.detectNet("ssd-mobilenet-v2", threshold=0.5)
camera = jetson.utils.videoSource("csi://0")      # or "/dev/video0" for USB webcam
display = jetson.utils.videoOutput("display://0") # or "my_video.mp4"

while display.IsStreaming():
    img = camera.Capture()
    detections = net.Detect(img)
    display.Render(img)
    display.SetStatus("Object Detection | Network &#123;:.0f&#125; FPS".format(net.GetNetworkFPS()))</pre>
